| `accountability.default_owner` | string or null | `platform-team` in keel and in a generated project; absent, null, which its reader reports as `[using default] accountability.default_owner = null` | one owner token of letters, digits and `._@-` (CONVENTIONS §12's grammar), never `TBD` or the word `null` in any letter case; or `null` | check_F and `scripts/jobs/build_corpus.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`, on every run | Names the owner a `kind: tool` or `kind: agent` document whose frontmatter `owner` is `TBD`, in any letter case, inherits, so check_F holds it owned; the corpus gives it to every node whose owner chain ends on a `TBD` (`owner_source: default`). `null`, or an absent key (the loader's default is `null`), gives no default: each such document is a check_F error naming it and this key, with no warning first. A value outside the grammar, or `TBD` or the word `null` in any letter case, is a check_F error naming the key on every run, whether or not a document needs it, and each such document's error then says the value was refused. | a document's own owner, which its frontmatter `owner` sets and the default never overrides; a node that names no owner, which the corpus keeps as `owner_source: none` and `scripts/accountability_report.py` lists | always |
